Below is a self-contained Rust function that replaces specific cells in one DataFrame (df0) with corresponding values from another DataFrame (df1), aligning rows by a key column. It uses the polars crate (modern, actively maintained; examples shown use the LazyFrame API). The function replaces df0[col] with df1[col] when df1 has a non-null value for that matching row. Non-null df1 values take precedence; otherwise df0 values are kept.

Notes:
- This example assumes the key column (on) exists in both df0 and df1.
- df1 columns are temporarily renamed with a suffix before the join so original names aren't clobbered.
- The function uses polars' lazy API to perform a left join and then per-column conditional replacement.

Cargo.toml (add to your project)
- polars versions are evolving; the example below uses a recent polars with lazy feature enabled. Adjust version as needed.

