        assert_eq!(out[0], vec!["name".to_string(), "age".to_string(), "city".to_string()]);
        assert_eq!(out[1][0], "Alice");
        assert_eq!(out[2][0], "Carol");
    }
}
```

Notes:
- This example uses Polars lazy execution (feature "lazy") to build and apply filters efficiently.
- Numeric comparisons require the condition value to be parseable as f64; equality will try numeric equality first and fall back to string equality if parsing fails.
- Conditions are ANDed; you can extend the design to support OR and grouped expressions by expanding the condition representation.

