Notes:
- Polars DataFrame does not maintain a separate index object like pandas; typically an "index" is modeled by columns. This function therefore:
  - Preserves any columns you indicate as the existing index (they remain regular columns).
  - Adds a fresh integer row index column (default name "index", made unique if needed).
  - Optionally reorders columns so existing index columns appear first (then the new integer index), followed by the other columns.
- If you don't have explicit index columns, call with_existing_index = None to just add a new integer index column.

Cargo dependency (add to Cargo.toml):
