- Binning rules: intervals are left-inclusive and right-exclusive: [b[i], b[i+1]), except the last interval is inclusive on the right: [b[n-2], b[n-1]].
- Values below the first boundary or NaN/unparseable strings become None (null) in the output interval column. You can easily change labels (e.g., "below", numeric bin index) by editing the label format.

